cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "us-federal-law: the in-force US federal law stack as structured data"
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
authors:
  - name: "Baja Labs"
repository-code: "https://github.com/bajalabs/us-federal-law"
license: CC0-1.0
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-10"
abstract: >-
  The Constitution of the United States, the United States Code (OLRC release
  point 119-138, titles and appendices), the Electronic Code of Federal Regulations
  (49 titles as of 2026-11-06) and the Public Laws of the 118th and 119th
  Congresses, mapped into one SQLite schema of laws, divisions, articles, parts,
  annotations and cross references, with full-text search. Built from the
  official sources with a sha256 manifest for every file.
keywords:
  - United States Code
  - Code of Federal Regulations
  - Constitution of the United States
  - Public Laws
  - legal data
  - open data
  - SQLite
